WEBVTT

1
00:02:34.390 --> 00:02:36.360
Hello, stranger.

2
00:03:11.520 --> 00:03:13.750
Sorry. Looking for a cigarette.

3
00:03:14.650 --> 00:03:15.980
I've given up.

4
00:03:18.690 --> 00:03:20.050
Thank you.

5
00:03:22.390 --> 00:03:24.620
- Got to be somewhere?N- Work.

6
00:03:26.160 --> 00:03:28.150
You didn't fancy my sandwiches?

7
00:03:28.270 --> 00:03:30.890
- Don't eat fish.N- Why not?

8
00:03:31.770 --> 00:03:33.460
Fish piss in the sea.

9
00:03:33.970 --> 00:03:36.800
- So do children.N- Don't eat children, either.

10
00:03:38.110 --> 00:03:39.600
What's your work?

11
00:03:39.680 --> 00:03:41.840
I'm sort of a journalist.

12
00:03:42.180 --> 00:03:45.010
- What sort?N- I write obituaries.

13
00:03:56.990 --> 00:03:59.160
Are we in for a long wait?

14
00:04:01.270 --> 00:04:03.390
She was 21 when she came in.

15
00:04:05.770 --> 00:04:07.260
Does it hurt?

16
00:04:07.970 --> 00:04:09.300
I'll live.

17
00:04:10.410 --> 00:04:12.870
Do you want me to put your leg up?

18
00:04:12.930 --> 00:04:14.490
Yes, please.

19
00:04:29.320 --> 00:04:31.310
Who cut off your crusts?

20
00:04:31.750 --> 00:04:32.740
Me.

21
00:04:32.820 --> 00:04:35.760
Did your mother cut off your crustsNwhen you were a little boy?

22
00:04:35.820 --> 00:04:39.190
- Yes, I believe she did.N- You should eat your crusts.

23
00:04:39.560 --> 00:04:41.460
You should stop smoking.

24
00:04:43.000 --> 00:04:44.490
How long was I out?

25
00:04:44.570 --> 00:04:47.130
- About 10 seconds.N- Then what?

26
00:04:48.400 --> 00:04:50.390
You came to. You focused on me.

27
00:04:50.470 --> 00:04:53.170
You said, "Hello, stranger."

28
00:04:53.240 --> 00:04:54.800
What a floozy.

29
00:04:54.880 --> 00:04:58.710
The cabbie crossed himself, he went,N"Thank fuck. I thought I'd killed her."

30
00:04:58.780 --> 00:05:01.150
I said, "Let's get her to a hospital."NHe hesitated.

31
00:05:01.220 --> 00:05:04.510
I think he thought there'd be paperworkNand he'd be held responsible.

32
00:05:04.590 --> 00:05:08.040
So I said with a slight sneer,N"Please just drop us at the hospital."

33
00:05:08.120 --> 00:05:09.710
Show me the sneer.

34
00:05:10.660 --> 00:05:12.630
Very good, buster.

35
00:05:13.690 --> 00:05:15.180
Thank you.

36
00:05:23.970 --> 00:05:26.240
- I told you, I've given up.N- Try harder.

37
00:05:26.310 --> 00:05:27.860
You live here?

38
00:05:28.280 --> 00:05:30.470
Just arrived from New York.

39
00:05:31.180 --> 00:05:33.110
Taking a vacation?

40
00:05:33.180 --> 00:05:35.080
I'm on an expedition.

41
00:05:35.720 --> 00:05:37.510
Where's your baggage?

42
00:05:38.650 --> 00:05:41.380
- Where are you staying?N- I'm a waif.

43
00:05:44.020 --> 00:05:45.500
A red bus.

44
00:05:47.250 --> 00:05:51.590
Policeman or "bobby."NObserve the distinctive helmet.

45
00:05:53.220 --> 00:05:55.750
Saint Paul's Cathedral.NPlease note the famous dome.

46
00:05:55.830 --> 00:05:59.660
- This is a truly magnificent tour.N- It's the London tourists never get to see.

47
00:05:59.730 --> 00:06:02.560
- What's this?N- I've no idea.

48
00:06:23.320 --> 00:06:27.090
They're all peopleNwho died saving the lives of others.

49
00:06:28.760 --> 00:06:30.660
I've been here before.

50
00:06:40.270 --> 00:06:43.100
Twenty years ago, we came here.

51
00:06:44.340 --> 00:06:48.330
My mother's dead. My father and I came hereNthe afternoon she died.

52
00:06:50.080 --> 00:06:53.780
She was a smoker.NShe died in the hospital, actually.

53
00:06:53.850 --> 00:06:56.580
- Is your father still alive?N- Hanging on.

54
00:06:57.020 --> 00:06:58.320
He's in a home.

55
00:06:58.960 --> 00:07:02.220
- You're late for work.N- You saying you want me to go?

56
00:07:02.290 --> 00:07:04.190
I'm saying you're late for work.

57
00:07:04.900 --> 00:07:07.460
How did you end up writing obituaries?

58
00:07:07.760 --> 00:07:11.890
Well, I had dreams of being a writer,Nbut I had no voice.

59
00:07:12.540 --> 00:07:14.900
What am I saying? I had no talent.

60
00:07:14.970 --> 00:07:19.230
So I ended up in obituaries,Nwhich is the Siberia of journalism.

61
00:07:19.470 --> 00:07:23.160
Tell me what you do.NI want to imagine you in Siberia.

62
00:07:23.240 --> 00:07:24.570
Really?

63
00:07:27.470 --> 00:07:30.310
We call it "the obits page."

64
00:07:31.350 --> 00:07:34.180
There's three of us: Me, Graham, and Harry.

65
00:07:34.780 --> 00:07:38.910
When I get to work, without fail...NAre you sure you want to know?

66
00:07:39.950 --> 00:07:44.050
Well, if someone important died,Nwe go to the "deep freeze"...

67
00:07:47.530 --> 00:07:51.050
which is a computer file...

68
00:07:51.130 --> 00:07:54.400
with all the obituaries,Nand we find the dead person's life.

69
00:07:54.470 --> 00:07:57.130
People's obituaries are writtenNwhile they're still alive?

70
00:07:57.200 --> 00:07:58.800
Some people's.

71
00:07:59.370 --> 00:08:02.430
Then Harry, he's the editor,Ndecides who we'll lead with.

72
00:08:02.510 --> 00:08:04.700
Then we make calls, check facts.

73
00:08:04.780 --> 00:08:09.340
At 6:00, we stand around the computerNand look at the next day's page...

74
00:08:10.150 --> 00:08:12.450
and make final changes.

75
00:08:12.790 --> 00:08:15.580
Add a few euphemismsNfor our own amusement.

76
00:08:15.660 --> 00:08:16.990
Such as?

77
00:08:19.260 --> 00:08:23.460
"He was a convivial fellow."NMeaning he was an alcoholic.

78
00:08:24.230 --> 00:08:27.630
"He valued his privacy." Gay.

79
00:08:28.100 --> 00:08:30.870
"He enjoyed his privacy." Raging queen.

80
00:08:32.070 --> 00:08:34.130
What would my euphemism be?

81
00:08:35.110 --> 00:08:38.100
- "She was disarming."N- That's not a euphemism.

82
00:08:38.980 --> 00:08:40.470
Yes, it is.

83
00:08:49.490 --> 00:08:52.380
- What were you doing in New York?N- You know.

84
00:08:55.520 --> 00:08:59.920
Well, no, I don't. What, were you studying?

85
00:09:00.090 --> 00:09:01.390
Stripping.

86
00:09:02.860 --> 00:09:05.090
Look at your little eyes.

87
00:09:06.200 --> 00:09:08.060
I can't see my little eyes.

88
00:09:13.500 --> 00:09:14.990
Why did you leave?

89
00:09:15.610 --> 00:09:17.600
Problems with a male.

90
00:09:17.870 --> 00:09:19.540
- Boyfriend?N- Kind of.

91
00:09:20.710 --> 00:09:22.940
And you left him, just like that?

92
00:09:23.010 --> 00:09:27.040
It's the only way to leave.N"I don't love you anymore. Goodbye."

93
00:09:27.120 --> 00:09:30.310
- Supposing you do still love them?N- You don't leave.

94
00:09:31.150 --> 00:09:34.320
- You've never left somebody you still love?N- No.

95
00:09:38.230 --> 00:09:39.790
This is me.

96
00:09:46.200 --> 00:09:47.860
Enjoy your stay.

97
00:09:49.210 --> 00:09:52.370
Please rememberNour traffic tends to come from the right.

98
00:09:54.140 --> 00:09:55.240
Bye.

99
00:10:08.060 --> 00:10:09.960
Do you have a girlfriend?

100
00:10:10.330 --> 00:10:11.660
Yeah. Ruth.

101
00:10:12.230 --> 00:10:15.200
She's called Ruth. She's a linguist.

102
00:10:16.600 --> 00:10:18.760
- What's your name?N- Alice.

103
00:10:19.900 --> 00:10:22.340
My name is Alice Ayres.

104
00:10:29.340 --> 00:10:30.500
Good.

105
00:10:30.600 --> 00:10:33.770
I'm just gonna change the film.NAre you okay for time?

106
00:10:37.910 --> 00:10:40.570
- Do you mind if I smoke?N- Lf you must.

107
00:10:41.750 --> 00:10:44.270
- I don't have to.N- Then don't.

108
00:10:56.400 --> 00:10:58.090
I liked your book.

109
00:10:59.000 --> 00:11:00.160
Thanks.

110
00:11:02.070 --> 00:11:04.970
- When's it published?N- Next year. How come you've read it?

111
00:11:05.040 --> 00:11:08.270
Your publisher sent me a manuscript.NI read it last night.

112
00:11:08.880 --> 00:11:10.810
You kept me up till 4:00.

113
00:11:11.850 --> 00:11:13.110
I'm flattered.

114
00:11:13.480 --> 00:11:15.950
Is your heroineNbased on someone you know?

115
00:11:16.520 --> 00:11:18.680
Yes. She's someone called Alice.

116
00:11:19.190 --> 00:11:21.680
How does she feelNabout you stealing her life?

117
00:11:21.760 --> 00:11:23.220
Borrowing her life.

118
00:11:23.360 --> 00:11:25.950
I'm dedicating the book to her.NShe's pleased.

119
00:11:34.870 --> 00:11:36.230
Do you exhibit?

120
00:11:36.300 --> 00:11:39.200
Sometimes. I have a thing next year.

121
00:11:45.210 --> 00:11:46.540
Portraits?

122
00:11:48.620 --> 00:11:51.210
- Of who?N- Strangers.

123
00:11:54.190 --> 00:11:57.670
How do your strangers feelNabout you stealing their lives?

124
00:11:57.850 --> 00:11:59.250
Borrowing.

125
00:12:00.820 --> 00:12:02.180
Am I a stranger?

126
00:12:03.120 --> 00:12:04.810
No. You're a job.

127
00:12:06.720 --> 00:12:08.780
And you're a sloucher. Sit up.

128
00:12:15.430 --> 00:12:16.900
You didn't find it obscene?

129
00:12:16.970 --> 00:12:18.560
- What?N- The book.

130
00:12:19.900 --> 00:12:22.030
I thought it was accurate.

131
00:12:22.670 --> 00:12:24.140
About what?

132
00:12:24.410 --> 00:12:26.740
About sex. About love.

133
00:12:27.080 --> 00:12:28.510
In what way?

134
00:12:28.980 --> 00:12:32.180
- You wrote it.N- You read it till 4:00.

135
00:12:32.520 --> 00:12:35.580
Don't raise your eyebrows.NIt makes you look smug.

136
00:12:43.890 --> 00:12:47.160
- But you did like it?N- Yes, but I could go off it.

137
00:12:53.600 --> 00:12:54.930
Stand up.

138
00:13:01.210 --> 00:13:03.040
Any criticisms?

139
00:13:04.650 --> 00:13:06.210
I'm not sure about the title.

140
00:13:06.280 --> 00:13:07.840
Got a better one?

141
00:13:08.790 --> 00:13:10.250
The Aquarium.

142
00:13:11.250 --> 00:13:12.980
So you liked the filth.

143
00:13:13.320 --> 00:13:16.050
- You like aquariums.N- Fish are therapeutic.

144
00:13:16.130 --> 00:13:18.490
- Hang out in aquariums, do you?N- When I can.

145
00:13:18.560 --> 00:13:20.390
Good for picking up strangers?

146
00:13:20.460 --> 00:13:22.800
Photographing strangers.

147
00:13:32.430 --> 00:13:33.760
Come here.

148
00:13:51.050 --> 00:13:52.710
You're beautiful.

149
00:14:00.390 --> 00:14:02.730
I don't kiss strange men.

150
00:14:03.130 --> 00:14:04.620
Neither do I.

151
00:15:15.960 --> 00:15:18.620
Do you and this Alice live together?

152
00:15:23.430 --> 00:15:24.760
Yes.

153
00:15:36.310 --> 00:15:37.710
Are you married?

154
00:15:37.780 --> 00:15:39.110
Yes.

155
00:15:39.350 --> 00:15:41.940
- No. Yes.N- Which?

156
00:15:42.290 --> 00:15:43.950
Separated.

157
00:15:44.590 --> 00:15:46.210
- Do you have any children?N- No.

158
00:15:46.290 --> 00:15:49.280
- Would you like some?N- Yes, but not today.

159
00:15:50.030 --> 00:15:52.360
Would Alice like children?

160
00:15:53.400 --> 00:15:54.920
She's too young.

161
00:15:56.130 --> 00:15:59.620
She works in a cafe near here.NShe's coming to meet me.

162
00:16:00.400 --> 00:16:01.800
Quite soon.

163
00:16:04.470 --> 00:16:06.810
Why are you wasting her time?

164
00:16:07.940 --> 00:16:10.780
- You're judgmental.N- You're devious.

165
00:16:10.850 --> 00:16:14.540
I'm not wasting her time.NShe's completely lovable.

166
00:16:14.620 --> 00:16:16.450
And completely unleavable.

167
00:16:16.520 --> 00:16:20.550
And you don't want someone elseNgetting their dirty hands on her.

168
00:16:20.660 --> 00:16:22.680
- Men are crap.N- But all the same...

169
00:16:22.760 --> 00:16:24.390
They're still crap.

170
00:16:26.160 --> 00:16:27.320
Your muse.

171
00:16:29.700 --> 00:16:32.690
- You've ruined my life.N- You'll get over it.

172
00:16:41.230 --> 00:16:42.390
Dan.

173
00:16:44.670 --> 00:16:46.000
Your shirt.

174
00:16:57.450 --> 00:16:59.150
You all done?

175
00:16:59.690 --> 00:17:02.310
- How's the photographer?N- Good. Professional.

176
00:17:03.320 --> 00:17:05.690
Rigorous. Beady. One of your lot.

177
00:17:05.760 --> 00:17:07.990
- What, female?N- Americano.

178
00:17:12.230 --> 00:17:13.560
Come on.

179
00:17:23.140 --> 00:17:24.370
Anna?

180
00:17:29.120 --> 00:17:30.780
- Alice.N- Hi.

181
00:17:30.850 --> 00:17:33.840
- Sorry to interrupt.N- No, we've just finished.

182
00:17:34.450 --> 00:17:36.480
- Would you like some tea?N- No, thanks.

183
00:17:36.560 --> 00:17:39.350
I've been serving it all day.NCan I use your loo?

184
00:17:39.430 --> 00:17:41.360
Sure. Just through there.

185
00:17:48.940 --> 00:17:50.230
She is beautiful.

186
00:17:50.300 --> 00:17:52.360
- I've got to see you.N- No.

187
00:17:52.840 --> 00:17:54.400
What's this? Patriotism?

188
00:17:54.470 --> 00:17:56.310
- I don't want trouble.N- I'm not trouble.

189
00:17:56.380 --> 00:17:57.780
You're taken.

190
00:17:59.910 --> 00:18:01.640
- I've got to see you.N- Tough.

191
00:18:01.710 --> 00:18:04.380
- You kissed me.N- What are you, 12?

192
00:18:07.740 --> 00:18:10.040
I'm a block of ice.

193
00:18:13.380 --> 00:18:15.180
Will you take my photo?

194
00:18:15.250 --> 00:18:17.950
I've never been photographedNby a professional before.

195
00:18:18.020 --> 00:18:20.620
I'd really appreciate it. I can pay you.

196
00:18:20.690 --> 00:18:22.420
No, I'd like to.

197
00:18:22.860 --> 00:18:24.690
Only if you don't mind.

198
00:18:25.300 --> 00:18:26.490
Why should I?

199
00:18:26.560 --> 00:18:28.550
Because you'll have to go away.

200
00:18:28.630 --> 00:18:31.460
We don't want him hereNwhile we're working, do we?

201
00:18:31.630 --> 00:18:33.120
No, we don't.

202
00:18:36.140 --> 00:18:38.330
Right. I'll be in the pub on the corner.

203
00:18:38.410 --> 00:18:39.640
Have fun.

204
00:18:42.880 --> 00:18:44.210
Thank you.

205
00:18:44.550 --> 00:18:47.810
- Good luck with your exhibition.N- Good luck with your book.

206
00:19:03.330 --> 00:19:05.530
So you've got an exhibition?

207
00:19:06.470 --> 00:19:07.630
Yeah.

208
00:19:12.180 --> 00:19:14.010
I read Dan's book.

209
00:19:15.110 --> 00:19:17.910
You've had quite a life.

210
00:19:19.350 --> 00:19:20.680
Thanks.

211
00:19:26.760 --> 00:19:28.920
He said you work in a cafe?

212
00:19:29.060 --> 00:19:30.890
I am a waitress.

213
00:19:31.230 --> 00:19:32.960
That's a temporary thing?

214
00:19:33.930 --> 00:19:34.920
No.

215
00:19:39.000 --> 00:19:41.480
Why don't you come over here and sit?

216
00:19:59.350 --> 00:20:01.810
- You live here?N- I do now.

217
00:20:02.080 --> 00:20:03.880
Because you're single?

218
00:20:04.480 --> 00:20:06.750
Who was your last boyfriend?

219
00:20:07.320 --> 00:20:08.580
My husband.

220
00:20:08.660 --> 00:20:10.250
Was he English?

221
00:20:10.660 --> 00:20:13.290
- Very.N- What happened to him?

222
00:20:14.860 --> 00:20:16.490
Someone younger.

223
00:20:18.830 --> 00:20:21.700
You've got a great face.

224
00:20:22.940 --> 00:20:24.600
Doesn't everyone?

225
00:20:25.970 --> 00:20:27.460
I suppose so.

226
00:20:27.840 --> 00:20:28.900
I just...

227
00:20:28.980 --> 00:20:31.910
From the book,Nsomehow I thought you'd be less...

228
00:20:32.380 --> 00:20:33.540
What?

229
00:20:36.550 --> 00:20:38.710
I don't know what, exactly.

230
00:20:51.630 --> 00:20:55.230
How do you feel about him using your life?

231
00:20:55.900 --> 00:20:58.370
It's really none of your business.

232
00:21:03.640 --> 00:21:06.080
When he let me in downstairs...

233
00:21:06.980 --> 00:21:08.640
he had this look.

234
00:21:11.050 --> 00:21:13.470
I just listened to your conversation.

235
00:21:18.210 --> 00:21:20.150
I don't know what to say.

236
00:21:23.990 --> 00:21:25.820
I'm not a thief, Alice.

237
00:21:32.860 --> 00:21:33.950
Do you want a drink?

238
00:21:34.030 --> 00:21:36.520
I have some vodka in the fridge.NWe could have a drink.

239
00:21:36.600 --> 00:21:38.430
Just take my picture.

240
00:21:58.960 --> 00:22:00.010
Good.

241
00:23:59.560 --> 00:24:00.660
Shit.

242
00:24:32.990 --> 00:24:34.820
What's the histology?

243
00:24:40.730 --> 00:24:42.060
Progressive?

244
00:24:42.800 --> 00:24:44.930
No. Sounds like an atrophy.

245
00:24:45.170 --> 00:24:46.830
Okay. Bye.

246
00:25:02.150 --> 00:25:03.480
Bollocks.

247
00:26:37.070 --> 00:26:38.400
Jesus.

248
00:29:18.440 --> 00:29:19.710
Anna?

249
00:29:23.880 --> 00:29:25.540
I got the coat.

250
00:29:26.320 --> 00:29:27.880
The white coat.

251
00:29:30.020 --> 00:29:31.350
So I see.

252
00:29:32.420 --> 00:29:34.760
I'm Larry. The doctor.

253
00:29:35.060 --> 00:29:36.360
Hello, Dr. Larry.

254
00:29:36.430 --> 00:29:39.360
Feel free to call me "The Sultan."

255
00:29:45.200 --> 00:29:48.170
I can't believe these things actually happen.

256
00:29:48.540 --> 00:29:51.010
I thought if you showed up,Nyou'd be an old trout.

257
00:29:51.080 --> 00:29:53.980
But you are bloody gorgeous.

258
00:29:54.950 --> 00:29:56.540
Well, thank you.

259
00:29:58.680 --> 00:30:01.480
Fish. You gotta respect them.

260
00:30:02.820 --> 00:30:04.650
- Have you?N- Of course.

261
00:30:05.290 --> 00:30:07.850
We were fish. Long ago.

262
00:30:08.260 --> 00:30:10.160
Before we were apes.

263
00:30:13.870 --> 00:30:15.800
You mentioned a hotel.

264
00:30:16.300 --> 00:30:17.790
No rush.

265
00:30:19.600 --> 00:30:22.900
Actually, there is.NI've got to be in surgery by 3:00.

266
00:30:23.610 --> 00:30:27.240
- Are you having an operation?N- No, I'm doing one.

267
00:30:28.080 --> 00:30:30.770
- Are you really a doctor?N- I said I was.

268
00:30:31.940 --> 00:30:33.600
You are Anna?

269
00:30:35.910 --> 00:30:39.370
I'm sorry. Did I photograph you?

270
00:30:39.710 --> 00:30:41.340
Did we meet somewhere?

271
00:30:41.420 --> 00:30:45.080
Come on. Don't play games,Nyou nymph of the Net.

272
00:30:45.520 --> 00:30:48.050
- Excuse me?N- You were up for it yesterday.

273
00:30:48.120 --> 00:30:51.420
- Was I?N- Yeah. "Wear my wet knickers.

274
00:30:52.390 --> 00:30:54.230
"Sit on my face.

275
00:30:55.260 --> 00:30:57.960
- "Cum-hungry bitch."N- Okay.

276
00:31:00.440 --> 00:31:02.630
Why do I feel like a pervert?

277
