I think you're the victim of a practical joke.

278
00:31:11.850 --> 00:31:14.440
- I am so sorry.N- It's okay.

279
00:31:18.590 --> 00:31:19.750
No.

280
00:31:21.190 --> 00:31:23.820
We spoke on the Net last night.NNow you've seen me...

281
00:31:23.890 --> 00:31:25.220
I wasn't on the Net last night.

282
00:31:25.290 --> 00:31:27.390
Where were youNbetween 6:45 and 7:00 p. M?

283
00:31:27.460 --> 00:31:29.050
That's really none of your business.

284
00:31:29.130 --> 00:31:32.100
- Where were you?N- On the Net, talking to you.

285
00:31:32.900 --> 00:31:36.500
- Well, I was talking to someone.N- Someone pretending to be me.

286
00:31:40.040 --> 00:31:42.640
I think you were talking to Daniel Woolf.

287
00:31:42.710 --> 00:31:45.770
- Who?N- This guy I know. It's him.

288
00:31:45.850 --> 00:31:48.280
- No, I was talking to a woman.N- How do you know?

289
00:31:48.350 --> 00:31:51.010
Believe me, she was a woman.NI got a huge...

290
00:31:51.090 --> 00:31:53.880
She was a... She wasn't, was she?

291
00:31:54.260 --> 00:31:55.420
No.

292
00:31:55.790 --> 00:31:57.660
What a bastard.

293
00:32:03.090 --> 00:32:04.820
How do you know him?

294
00:32:04.890 --> 00:32:09.020
I don't really know him.NI took his photograph for a book he wrote.

295
00:32:09.090 --> 00:32:11.890
- I hope it sank without a trace.N- It's on its way.

296
00:32:11.960 --> 00:32:14.160
There is justice in the world.

297
00:32:14.700 --> 00:32:16.360
What's it called?

298
00:32:25.740 --> 00:32:27.180
The Aquarium.

299
00:32:27.250 --> 00:32:30.580
What a prick! He's advertising.

300
00:32:32.620 --> 00:32:35.180
But why would he pretend to be you?

301
00:32:36.120 --> 00:32:37.610
I think he likes me.

302
00:32:37.720 --> 00:32:40.350
Funny way of showing it.NCan't he send you flowers?

303
00:32:40.430 --> 00:32:43.050
Extraordinary thing, the Internet.

304
00:32:43.260 --> 00:32:46.030
Possibility of genuineNglobal communication.

305
00:32:46.430 --> 00:32:48.560
The first great democratic medium.

306
00:32:48.630 --> 00:32:51.330
Absolutely. It's the future.

307
00:32:51.740 --> 00:32:54.070
Two guys wanking in cyberspace.

308
00:32:54.470 --> 00:32:56.240
He was the wanker.

309
00:32:57.680 --> 00:33:00.010
I'll say this for him, he can write.

310
00:33:01.610 --> 00:33:02.980
Is he in love with you?

311
00:33:03.050 --> 00:33:05.280
I don't know. No.

312
00:33:05.850 --> 00:33:08.680
- Are you in love with him?N- I hardly know him.

313
00:33:08.750 --> 00:33:10.910
But you're sort of interested.

314
00:33:11.060 --> 00:33:13.390
I think he's interesting.

315
00:33:13.690 --> 00:33:16.160
No, don't. I look like a criminal in photos.

316
00:33:16.230 --> 00:33:18.130
Please. It's my birthday.

317
00:33:18.360 --> 00:33:19.490
Really?

318
00:33:20.300 --> 00:33:21.560
Really.

319
00:33:35.940 --> 00:33:37.230
Happy birthday.

320
00:33:40.410 --> 00:33:41.470
Thank you.

321
00:33:42.180 --> 00:33:44.980
This man comes into the cafe todayNand he says:

322
00:33:45.050 --> 00:33:48.140
"Hey, waitress, what are you waiting for?"

323
00:33:48.620 --> 00:33:49.950
Funny guy.

324
00:33:50.390 --> 00:33:53.880
So I go,N"I'm waiting for a man to come in here...

325
00:33:54.320 --> 00:33:57.850
"and fuck me sidewaysNwith a beautiful line like that."

326
00:33:58.260 --> 00:33:59.750
What did he do?

327
00:33:59.830 --> 00:34:02.390
Asked for a cup of tea with two sugars.

328
00:34:13.940 --> 00:34:16.380
- I'm waiting for you.N- To do what?

329
00:34:18.580 --> 00:34:19.910
Leave me.

330
00:34:20.880 --> 00:34:24.750
I'm not going to leave you.NI totally love you. Why is this?

331
00:34:25.820 --> 00:34:28.950
Please let me come.NI want to be there for you.

332
00:34:29.620 --> 00:34:32.490
- Are you ashamed of me?N- Of course not. I told you...

333
00:34:32.560 --> 00:34:34.960
- I want to be alone.N- Why?

334
00:34:37.100 --> 00:34:38.620
To grieve.

335
00:34:39.400 --> 00:34:40.890
To think.

336
00:34:43.470 --> 00:34:46.630
- I love you. Why won't you let me?N- It's only a weekend.

337
00:34:46.910 --> 00:34:49.170
Why won't you let me love you?

338
00:34:52.750 --> 00:34:54.080
Buster.

339
00:35:00.020 --> 00:35:01.890
Let's go to this thing...

340
00:35:02.090 --> 00:35:04.820
then I'll get my train. I'll be away one night.

341
00:35:05.160 --> 00:35:07.810
I'll be back before you know it, okay?

342
00:35:37.620 --> 00:35:39.850
Do these people pay you?NOr do you pay them?

343
00:36:06.140 --> 00:36:07.480
Like it?

344
00:36:10.250 --> 00:36:11.580
No.

345
00:36:13.690 --> 00:36:15.740
What were you so sad about?

346
00:36:16.690 --> 00:36:19.050
- Life.N- What's that, then?

347
00:36:22.360 --> 00:36:25.260
So what do you reckon, in general?

348
00:36:25.630 --> 00:36:27.430
You want to talk about art?

349
00:36:27.500 --> 00:36:30.900
I know it's vulgar to discuss The WorkNat an opening of The Work...

350
00:36:30.970 --> 00:36:33.100
but someone's got to do it.

351
00:36:35.110 --> 00:36:37.570
I'm serious. What do you think?

352
00:36:38.780 --> 00:36:40.260
It's a lie.

353
00:36:40.940 --> 00:36:44.560
It's a bunch of sad strangersNphotographed beautifully...

354
00:36:45.040 --> 00:36:49.370
and all the glittering assholesNwho appreciate art...

355
00:36:49.680 --> 00:36:53.170
say it's beautifulNbecause that's what they want to see.

356
00:36:53.250 --> 00:36:55.740
But the people in the photos are sad...

357
00:36:56.620 --> 00:36:57.980
and alone.

358
00:36:58.050 --> 00:37:01.720
But the picturesNmake the world seem beautiful...

359
00:37:01.790 --> 00:37:06.190
so the exhibition's reassuring,Nwhich makes it a lie.

360
00:37:06.730 --> 00:37:09.390
And everyone loves a big, fat lie.

361
00:37:09.830 --> 00:37:13.390
- I'm the big, fat liar's boyfriend.N- Bastard.

362
00:37:13.470 --> 00:37:15.440
- Larry.N- Alice.

363
00:37:18.540 --> 00:37:20.200
So you're Anna's boyfriend.

364
00:37:20.280 --> 00:37:22.140
A princess can kiss a toad.

365
00:37:22.210 --> 00:37:23.300
- Frog.N- Toad.

366
00:37:23.380 --> 00:37:26.540
- Frog.N- Toad, frog, lobster. They're all the same.

367
00:37:27.920 --> 00:37:30.410
So how long have you been seeing her?

368
00:37:30.490 --> 00:37:33.220
Four months. We're in the first flush.

369
00:37:33.920 --> 00:37:37.590
It's paradise. All my nasty habits amuse her.

370
00:37:37.890 --> 00:37:40.120
- You shouldn't smoke.N- Fuck off.

371
00:37:40.190 --> 00:37:42.750
I'm a doctor.NI'm supposed to say things like that.

372
00:37:42.830 --> 00:37:44.730
- You want one?N- No.

373
00:37:45.530 --> 00:37:47.190
Yes. No.

374
00:37:47.570 --> 00:37:49.260
Fuck it, yes.

375
00:37:50.040 --> 00:37:51.370
No.

376
00:37:52.870 --> 00:37:54.360
I've given up.

377
00:37:56.710 --> 00:37:59.610
Anna tells me your bloke wrote a book.

378
00:37:59.680 --> 00:38:02.380
- Any good?N- Of course.

379
00:38:02.980 --> 00:38:04.980
It's about you, isn't it?

380
00:38:05.490 --> 00:38:08.650
- Some of me.N- Oh? What did he leave out?

381
00:38:09.960 --> 00:38:11.620
The truth.

382
00:38:12.560 --> 00:38:14.250
Is he here, your bloke?

383
00:38:14.320 --> 00:38:17.410
Yeah, he's over there talking to your bird.

384
00:38:20.960 --> 00:38:22.860
My boyfriend's here.

385
00:38:23.860 --> 00:38:25.520
He's here? Where?

386
00:38:27.370 --> 00:38:28.530
There.

387
00:38:29.530 --> 00:38:30.870
With Alice?

388
00:38:31.340 --> 00:38:33.500
I believe you're acquainted.

389
00:38:37.810 --> 00:38:40.610
- I've never seen him before.N- No.

390
00:38:41.780 --> 00:38:43.180
But you've spoken.

391
00:38:43.510 --> 00:38:45.510
Well, conversed.

392
00:38:46.380 --> 00:38:48.940
- Corresponded.N- I wrote to him?

393
00:38:49.720 --> 00:38:53.780
On the Net. You sent him to the aquarium.NI happened to be there.

394
00:38:54.530 --> 00:38:56.320
Nice work, Cupid.

395
00:39:00.200 --> 00:39:03.070
- We need to talk about this.N- No, we don't.

396
00:39:03.200 --> 00:39:04.760
He's very pretty.

397
00:39:05.800 --> 00:39:08.470
She is very tall.

398
00:39:13.510 --> 00:39:15.450
So you're a stripper?

399
00:39:16.250 --> 00:39:17.410
Yeah.

400
00:39:18.150 --> 00:39:19.310
And?

401
00:39:42.210 --> 00:39:43.870
You take care, now.

402
00:39:44.240 --> 00:39:45.540
I will.

403
00:39:45.930 --> 00:39:47.370
You, too.

404
00:39:55.780 --> 00:39:58.270
That's the way it should be.

405
00:40:01.920 --> 00:40:03.410
He's very funny.

406
00:40:08.490 --> 00:40:10.420
Excuse me. Nice to meet you.

407
00:40:17.500 --> 00:40:19.970
- Pleased with the success?N- Yes, absolutely.

408
00:40:20.800 --> 00:40:22.790
Yours was the best.

409
00:40:23.270 --> 00:40:25.300
You were the belle of the bullshit.

410
00:40:25.370 --> 00:40:27.070
Who were those awful people?

411
00:40:27.140 --> 00:40:30.240
- Where do they come from?N- Why should we care?

412
00:40:34.380 --> 00:40:37.820
- You get this one. You'll miss your train.N- I'll be fine.

413
00:40:38.350 --> 00:40:39.840
Come on, it's cold.

414
00:40:46.360 --> 00:40:48.190
I'll see you on Sunday.

415
00:40:53.530 --> 00:40:55.020
Where to, love?

416
00:40:59.210 --> 00:41:00.370
Taxi!

417
00:41:11.520 --> 00:41:12.680
Sorry.

418
00:41:13.020 --> 00:41:15.680
Why don't you make upNyour bleeding mind?

419
00:41:21.290 --> 00:41:24.120
Thank you so much.NI appreciate your coming.

420
00:41:24.190 --> 00:41:26.450
I'll call you tomorrow. See you next week.

421
00:41:26.520 --> 00:41:28.460
- Thanks.N- Thanks very much.

422
00:41:31.860 --> 00:41:34.200
- I thought you'd gone.N- I forgot this.

423
00:41:36.370 --> 00:41:40.300
So he's a dermatologist.NCan you get more boring than that?

424
00:41:40.370 --> 00:41:43.340
- Obituarist?N- Failed novelist, please.

425
00:41:44.180 --> 00:41:45.940
I was sorry about your book.

426
00:41:46.010 --> 00:41:48.170
Thanks. I blame the title.

427
00:41:48.480 --> 00:41:51.680
So we pull out our Christmas crackersNwith those appalling jokes.

428
00:41:51.750 --> 00:41:54.450
My guy says,N"Hang on. These are second-rate jokes.

429
00:41:54.520 --> 00:41:58.010
"I've got a first-rate joke.NSit back and take notice."

430
00:41:58.090 --> 00:42:00.890
So we go, "Okay, what's the joke?"NAnd he says:

431
00:42:01.160 --> 00:42:02.920
"It's based on A Christmas Carol...

432
00:42:02.990 --> 00:42:05.360
"which is why it seemsNso relevant on Christmas Day."

433
00:42:05.430 --> 00:42:07.800
I haven't even seen you for a year.

434
00:42:07.870 --> 00:42:08.990
Yes, you have.

435
00:42:09.070 --> 00:42:11.470
Only because you stalk meNoutside my studio.

436
00:42:11.540 --> 00:42:13.600
I don't stalk. I lurk.

437
00:42:13.670 --> 00:42:15.870
And when I'm not there you look for me.

438
00:42:15.940 --> 00:42:19.430
- How do you know if you're not there?N- Because I am there...

439
00:42:20.110 --> 00:42:21.810
lurking from a distance.

440
00:42:30.490 --> 00:42:31.820
Look at me.

441
00:42:32.560 --> 00:42:34.720
Tell me you're not in love with me.

442
00:42:35.490 --> 00:42:37.650
I'm not in love with you.

443
00:42:40.300 --> 00:42:41.960
You just lied.

444
00:42:48.340 --> 00:42:50.930
I'm your stranger. Jump.

445
00:43:19.290 --> 00:43:22.060
- Hello, stranger.N- Hello.

446
00:43:22.730 --> 00:43:24.720
Intense conversation?

447
00:43:27.100 --> 00:43:28.930
His father died.

448
00:43:30.040 --> 00:43:31.530
Were you spying?

449
00:43:31.610 --> 00:43:33.470
Lovingly observing...

450
00:43:33.740 --> 00:43:35.300
with a telescope.

451
00:43:37.610 --> 00:43:39.670
He's taller than in his photo.

452
00:43:40.280 --> 00:43:42.110
His photo's a headshot.

453
00:43:42.180 --> 00:43:43.780
Yeah, I know.

454
00:43:43.850 --> 00:43:47.790
But his head implied a short body,Nwhen, in fact, his head is deceptive.

455
00:43:47.990 --> 00:43:49.010
Deceptive?

456
00:43:49.090 --> 00:43:52.490
He's actually got a long body.NHe's a stringy fucker.

457
00:43:53.630 --> 00:43:55.190
I could have him.

458
00:43:56.160 --> 00:43:59.660
- What?N- Lf it came to it, in a scrap, I could have him.

459
00:44:01.100 --> 00:44:03.540
Did you tell him we call him Cupid?

460
00:44:04.240 --> 00:44:07.000
No, that's our joke.

461
00:44:08.940 --> 00:44:11.210
I had a chat with young Alice.

462
00:44:11.280 --> 00:44:13.010
- Fancy her?N- Of course.

463
00:44:13.110 --> 00:44:14.840
- Not as much as you.N- Why not?

464
00:44:14.920 --> 00:44:16.880
You're a woman. She's a girl.

465
00:44:16.950 --> 00:44:20.440
She has the moronic beauty of youth,Nbut she's sly.

466
00:44:20.690 --> 00:44:24.170
- She seems open to me.N- That's how she wants to seem.

467
00:44:24.250 --> 00:44:27.780
You forget you're dealing withNa clinical observer of the human carnival.

468
00:44:27.850 --> 00:44:29.680
- Am I, now?N- Yes.

469
00:44:29.750 --> 00:44:33.690
You seem more like the catNthat got the cream. Stop licking yourself.

470
00:44:39.330 --> 00:44:42.490
That's the nastiest thingNyou've ever said to me.

471
00:44:46.000 --> 00:44:47.600
That's horrible.

472
00:44:47.840 --> 00:44:49.310
I'm sorry.

473
00:44:50.680 --> 00:44:52.340
I'm so sorry.

474
00:45:40.560 --> 00:45:43.430
- Where have you been?N- Work thing.

475
00:45:44.500 --> 00:45:47.490
Had a drink with Harry.NYou never have one drink with Harry.

476
00:45:47.570 --> 00:45:50.530
- You know he's in love with you.N- No, he's not.

477
00:45:51.540 --> 00:45:52.830
Is he?

478
00:45:54.710 --> 00:45:56.400
Did you eat?

479
00:45:56.670 --> 00:45:58.890
I'll make you something.

480
00:45:59.770 --> 00:46:01.430
I'm not hungry.

481
00:46:23.490 --> 00:46:24.550
What?

482
00:46:28.260 --> 00:46:29.750
This will hurt.

483
00:46:30.770 --> 00:46:32.490
I've been with Anna.

484
00:46:33.330 --> 00:46:35.030
I'm in love with her.

485
00:46:36.070 --> 00:46:38.700
We've been seeing each other for a year.

486
00:46:39.040 --> 00:46:41.010
It began at her opening.

487
00:46:57.160 --> 00:46:59.320
- Have a nice one.N- Cheers, guvnor.

488
00:47:22.050 --> 00:47:23.380
Don't move.

489
00:47:24.390 --> 00:47:26.440
I want to remember this moment forever.

490
00:47:26.520 --> 00:47:29.840
First time I walked through the door,Nreturning from a business trip...

491
00:47:29.910 --> 00:47:32.710
to be greeted by my wife.

492
00:47:33.180 --> 00:47:35.880
I have, in this moment, become an adult.

493
00:47:36.150 --> 00:47:38.710
Thanks for waiting up, you darling.

494
00:47:40.490 --> 00:47:42.150
You goddess.

495
00:47:46.400 --> 00:47:47.990
I missed you.

496
00:47:48.400 --> 00:47:50.090
How about some tea?

497
00:47:50.470 --> 00:47:52.460
Jesus, I'm knackered!

498
00:47:52.540 --> 00:47:54.560
- Didn't you sleep on the plane?N- No...

499
00:47:54.640 --> 00:47:58.700
because the permed German next to meNwas snoring like a Messerschmitt.

500
00:47:58.780 --> 00:48:01.180
- What's the time?N- About midnight.

501
00:48:01.310 --> 00:48:03.750
Time. What a tricky little fucker.

502
00:48:04.480 --> 00:48:07.820
My head's in two places.NMy brain actually hurts.

503
00:48:07.890 --> 00:48:10.880
- Do you want some food?N- No, I need a bath.

504
00:48:11.320 --> 00:48:14.450
- I'll run it for you.N- No, I'll have a shower.

505
00:48:14.830 --> 00:48:16.160
You okay?

506
00:48:16.890 --> 00:48:18.290
How was the thing?

507
00:48:18.360 --> 00:48:21.530
As dermatological conferences go,Nit was a riot.

508
00:48:22.430 --> 00:48:24.030
How was the hotel?

509
00:48:24.370 --> 00:48:28.000
Someone told me thatNthe beautiful people of the Paranoid Hotel...

510
00:48:28.070 --> 00:48:32.010
the concierge, the bellboys and girls...NDid you know this?

511
00:48:32.310 --> 00:48:35.110
- They're all whores.N- Everybody knows that.

512
00:48:35.780 --> 00:48:36.940
I didn't.

513
00:48:39.550 --> 00:48:42.540
I don't suppose you'd fancy a friendly poke.

514
00:48:42.990 --> 00:48:44.650
I just had a bath.

515
00:48:46.190 --> 00:48:47.520
Right.

516
00:48:48.160 --> 00:48:51.090
I'll see to myself, then,Nin the Elle Decoration bathroom.

517
00:48:51.160 --> 00:48:54.690
- You chose that bathroom.N- And every time I wash in it I feel dirty.

518
00:48:54.770 --> 00:48:57.200
It's cleaner than I am. It's got attitude.

519
00:48:57.270 --> 00:48:59.240
The mirror says, "Who the fuck are you?"

520
00:48:59.300 --> 00:49:01.970
- You chose it.N- Doesn't mean I like it.

521
00:49:02.140 --> 00:49:03.990
We shouldn't have this.

522
00:49:04.060 --> 00:49:05.900
I hear middle-class guilt.

523
00:49:05.970 --> 00:49:09.900
Working-class guilt.NWhy are you dressed if you just had a bath?

524
00:49:11.470 --> 00:49:13.170
We needed some milk.

525
00:49:14.280 --> 00:49:15.500
You okay?

526
00:49:16.540 --> 00:49:18.270
- You?N- Yeah.

527
00:49:22.520 --> 00:49:23.850
I'm going.

528
00:49:24.190 --> 00:49:26.520
- I'm sorry.N- Irrelevant.

529
00:49:27.720 --> 00:49:29.550
What are you sorry for?

530
00:49:29.860 --> 00:49:31.350
